{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world holds data: entities and their components, and resources. A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"system","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" holds a rule: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"step that reads part of the world and changes part of it, such as “every entity with a velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves” or “gravity pulls on everything that isn’t frozen.” A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"schedule"}]},{"type":"text","text":" lists the systems of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frame or step and runs them on a world, each once per run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and event:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double, y: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double, dy: Double }","struct Health: Component { var current: Int }","struct Frozen: Component {}","","struct Score: Resource { var points: Int }","struct TimeStep: Resource { var seconds: Double }","struct Paused: Resource {}","","struct Damage: Event { var target: Entity, amount: Int }"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Declare a System","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Declare-a-System"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The simplest way to write a system is to mark a type with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@System"},{"type":"text","text":" macro and give it a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method. The method’s parameters say what the system works on, and their types say how:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update"},{"type":"text","text":" writes components, a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query"},{"type":"text","text":" reads them, and a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reads a resource. The following two systems pull everything that isn’t frozen downward, then move"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it by its velocity:"}]},{"code":["@System","struct Gravity {","    func run(_ falling: Update<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        falling { velocity, _ in velocity.dy -= 10 }","    }","}","","@System","struct Movement {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","            position.y += row.components.dy","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because the parameters’ types state what each system reads and writes, the macro writes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for you: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gravity"},{"text":" writes ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Movement"},{"text":" writes ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Position"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Velocity"},{"text":". A schedule uses the access to decide which systems can run at the same time.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can also conform a type to "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"},{"type":"text","text":" by hand and write its "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)"},{"type":"text","text":" method, which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"receives the whole world. See "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"},{"type":"text","text":" for when to do that."}]},{"text":"Run Systems in a Schedule","type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Run-Systems-in-a-Schedule"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is built from a list of systems, written in a result builder. Running it runs each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"system once. The following example drops a ball for one frame:"}]},{"code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 90.0)\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems run in the order you write them, unless an ordering constraint says otherwise.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"after(_:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"before(_:)"},{"text":" require one system to run after or before another; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names a group of systems so constraints can refer to all of them at once; and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"runIf(_:)"},{"text":" skips","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a system when a condition doesn’t hold.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems whose accesses don’t conflict, because neither writes what the other reads or writes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run at the same time, and the world ends as though they had run one after another (commands","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apply when each wave finishes). Systems that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conflict run in order. When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, their order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rests only on how they happen to be written; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" finds those pairs so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"test can keep a schedule free of them.","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"externalID":"Systems","role":"collection","title":"Systems","modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"symbolKind":"module","roleHeading":"Framework"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"]},{"title":"System Parameters","anchor":"System-Parameters","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"]},{"title":"Building and Running Schedules","anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"]},{"title":"Main-Actor Systems","anchor":"Main-Actor-Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"]},{"title":"Built-In Systems","anchor":"Built-In-Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges"]},{"title":"Profiling","anchor":"Profiling","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule."}],"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/CyclicOrdering":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"CyclicOrdering","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An error indicating that the ordering constraints of a schedule’s systems form a cycle, so no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order satisfies them all."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/cyclicordering","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"CyclicOrdering"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceReader":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceReader"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ResourceReader"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcereader","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads a resource."}],"title":"ResourceReader","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DeclaringSystems":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write the rules of a simulation as systems, and let their parameters state what they read and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"write."}],"type":"topic","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Declaring Systems","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/declaringsystems"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/RemovedComponents":{"title":"RemovedComponents","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RemovedComponents"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RemovedComponents"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A system parameter that lists the entities that lost a component since the system last read","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/removedcomponents","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Query":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/query","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A description of the entities to visit and the components to read from each."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Query"}],"title":"Query","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Query"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemSet":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that names a group of systems, so ordering constraints can refer to all of them at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"title":"SystemSet","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemSet"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemSet"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemset"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduleBuilder":{"title":"ScheduleBuilder","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScheduleBuilder","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScheduleBuilder","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A result builder that collects the systems written in a "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"’s closure."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulebuilder","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduledSystem":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduledSystem"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduledSystem"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system together with the ordering constraints, sets and conditions a schedule runs it with."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/scheduledsystem","kind":"symbol","title":"ScheduledSystem"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp":{"title":"Driving a World from an App","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/drivingaworldfromanapp","abstract":[{"text":"Hold a world in your app or game engine, feed it each frame’s input, and let the objects outside","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it read results and take part in a step.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","type":"topic","kind":"article"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System()":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"macro","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"()","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system()","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Makes a type a system whose access comes from the parameters of its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method."}],"title":"System()","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems":{"url":"\/documentation\/systems","title":"Systems","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventReader":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EventReader","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads the events of one type sent since the system last read them."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventreader","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"EventReader"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/EventWriter":{"title":"EventWriter","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventWriter"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EventWriter"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that sends events of one type."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/eventwriter","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/MainActorSystem":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A system that runs on the main actor, for work that touches main-actor state such as a user","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interface.","type":"text"}],"title":"MainActorSystem","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MainActorSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MainActorSystem","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/mainactorsystem"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardChanges":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A system that yields each component of one type added or changed since it last ran to an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"asynchronous stream, with its entity.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardChanges"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardChanges"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"ForwardChanges","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardchanges"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/run(in:)":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"run","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"in","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"inout","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"World","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule0A0V"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"required":true,"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/run(in:)","title":"run(in:)","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Runs the system’s rule once on a world."}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Schedule"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"title":"Schedule","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/UpdateEvents":{"title":"UpdateEvents","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UpdateEvents"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UpdateEvents"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that ends the current event update, dropping events old enough that every reader"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"has had its chance to read them."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/updateevents","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemTiming":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemTiming"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemTiming"}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemtiming","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The times one system of a schedule has taken to run."}],"title":"SystemTiming","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule/ambiguities()":{"title":"ambiguities()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ambiguities"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Systems9AmbiguityV"},{"text":"]","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Returns every pair of systems whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"orders."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule\/ambiguities()","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Ambiguity":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Ambiguity","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Two systems of a schedule whose accesses conflict but that no ordering constraint orders, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the order they run in rests only on the order they were written in.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/ambiguity","kind":"symbol","title":"Ambiguity"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","title":"Update","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemParameter":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemParameter"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SystemParameter"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type a system’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"type":"text","text":" method can take in place of the whole world, whose type states what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the system reads and writes."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemparameter","title":"SystemParameter","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardEvents":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardEvents"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardEvents"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that yields each event of one type to an asynchronous stream, so code outside the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"schedule can await the events."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardevents","title":"ForwardEvents","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ResourceWriter":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ResourceWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ResourceWriter","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that reads and writes a resource."}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/resourcewriter","kind":"symbol","title":"ResourceWriter"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"System"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A rule that reads and changes a world, run once each time its schedule runs.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system","kind":"symbol","title":"System"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemProfile":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemProfile","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A resource that records how long each system takes to run."}],"url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemprofile","title":"SystemProfile","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/System/access":{"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic","required":true,"title":"access","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/system\/access","abstract":[{"text":"The component, resource and event types the system reads and writes, or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"text":" if it may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change anything.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"access"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11WorldModule6AccessV","text":"Access"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access","defaultImplementations":1}}}